course: dictionary
lesson: 10037
title: Words about words
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: «Terminological» sounds big, but it comes from «term», a special word used in one subject. A term is the right name for a thing in a subject, such as numerator in maths.
explain: A terminological question is a question about words and their names: which word should we use? For example, is the top number of a fraction called the numerator or the denominator? The answer is the numerator.
explain: Teachers, writers and dictionary makers use this word when they talk about the right words for things. They are not usually being funny. They are being careful.
explain: Adults sometimes joke with it too: «"Terminological inexactitude" is a joking name for a lie.» It sounds clever and polite, but it just means a lie, so take the joke with a smile.
fact: Terminological means to do with terms, the special words used in a subject.
fact: «Terminology» is the noun: the special words used in a subject, such as the terminology of maths.
fact: «Terminologically» is the adverb: in a way that is about terms and their meanings.
fact: «Terminological inexactitude» is a joking, polite way to say a lie, used mostly in the UK.
fact: Numerator and denominator are maths terms: the numerator is the top number of a fraction.
exercise: Which word means to do with the special words used in a subject? | Tiny | *Terminological | Hungry | Dreamy
exercise: Which maths term is the top number of a fraction? | *Numerator | Product | Denominator | Remainder
exercise: Tom says, «It was never late, it was a terminological inexactitude.» What does he really mean? | *He is telling a lie | He is very tired | He has a new watch | He is telling the truth about the time
test: Which word is the noun for the special words used in a subject? | Terminally | Terminological | Terminal | *Terminology
test: Which phrase is a polite, joking way to say a lie? | Terminology book | *Terminological inexactitude | Terminal station | Terminal sickness
exam: Which best describes a terminological question? | A question about your favourite colour | A question about how fast you can run | A question about the weather | *A question about which word is the right name for something
